  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "W8Yrjo3qD+xz2YpQpgghJ62Ul0U=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:20.712Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "This proposal has two halves and only one of them is an integration. The integration half is a Django signal dispatching typed operations from Abilian SBE. The other half is distribution: Switchboard packaged as a Nua-deployable service, which makes the record layer an item in the partner's own platform-as-a-service catalogue.\n\nThat second half is a different kind of move from anything else in this part of the corpus. Every other group proposes a demo that shows a capability; this one proposes that the capability become part of what the partner already sells and operates. The integration then serves as the worked example of a catalogue entry rather than as the deliverable itself.\n\nThe single lead is Abilian in Paris, marked \"2 \u00b7 next\". The metasfresh group makes a similar argument from the reseller side \u2014 ship inside the partner's channel, not beside it \u2014 which suggests the distribution framing is worth generalising to partners who run their own platform or store.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- Abilian (FR Paris) \u2014 St\u00e9fane Fermigier, directeur de la publication \u00b7 contact@abilian.com \u00b7 https://abilian.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Switchboard packaged as a Nua-deployable service, plus a Django signal dispatching typed operations from Abilian SBE \u2014 makes the record layer part of their own PaaS catalogue.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:20.712905Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:20.712910Z"
    }
  },
